      "fact": "Protocol mode 4 selects RADIO.MODE=9 (nRF4Mbit0BT6); distinct from protocol mode 2 selecting RADIO.MODE=4. These two numeric mode namespaces must not be confused."
    },
    {
      "id": "uplink-check",
      "confidence": "high-assembly-crosschecked",
      "evidence": [
        "mouse 23024BAA..23024BF4",
        "dongle 2302427A..230242BC"
      ],
      "fact": "Normal mouse DMA frame [L,data L bytes] becomes [L+1,data,(-sum(data)) mod256]. Receiver requires HW CRCOK and nonzero Lwire; sums bytes 1..Lwire-1, compares byte Lwire, restores length Lwire-1. Length field and hardware CRC excluded."
    },
    {
      "id": "decompiler-alias-correction",
      "confidence": "high-assembly-crosschecked",
      "evidence": [
        "mouse 23024BB8 str.w ip,[r0]",
        "mouse 23024BD4 ldrb.w r1,[r2,#1]!"
      ],
      "fact": "Full first source word is stored before checksum. Ghidra global alias output appears to restore it afterwards; use assembly ordering."
    },
    {
      "id": "downlink-no-extra-check",
      "confidence": "high-assembly-crosschecked",
      "evidence": [
        "dongle 230248D6..230248F4",
        "mouse 23021704 C lines 240..355"
      ],
      "fact": "Recovered normal downlink copies 16 bytes unchanged and assigns PACKETPTR; no additive append. Mouse mode4 RX accepts CRCOK path without additive verification. This does not describe other protocol modes."
