      "fact": "Changed uplink link-sequence resets miss bookkeeping and pops selected downlink queue iff queue<6, advancing TX sequence1..7. Duplicate still stores packet and calls notification; cannot infer global duplicate suppression from this function."
    },
    {
      "id": "mouse-ack",
      "confidence": "high",
      "evidence": [
        "mouse 23021704 C lines270..333"
      ],
      "fact": "CRCOK mode4 downlink advances uplink sequence1..7, clears miss counter and motion cache, marks ack flag and pops selected queue if <6. CRC failure retains sequence/cache, increments failure bookkeeping, sets retry holdoff DAT_230029D0=2."
    },
    {
      "id": "counter-sync",
      "confidence": "high-assembly-crosschecked",
      "evidence": [
        "mouse 23024846..23024898"
      ],
      "fact": "Only byte3==1F updates event counter: capture7 in166..249 => received BE16;416..499=>received+1 modulo65536;else keep old. Unsigned32 range tests."
    },
    {
      "id": "disconnect",
      "confidence": "high",
      "evidence": [
        "mouse 2302243C C lines1229..1303",
        "dongle 23021BBC C lines583..619"
      ],
      "fact": "At end slot5 in connected states, increment event/miss counters; >=100 missed-cycle counter stops link; data-gap >=200 changes connection-state3->4 if miss<100. Units are scheduler cycles; thresholds are not number of individual retransmissions."
    }
